--- 17:00 host budget closure（五个块数，同一 kernel 形状）---

probe_hostbudget.py.  wall = time.perf_counter over 50 enqueues, no sync
inside.  prof = cProfile total for the same 50 calls.

  blocks       N    block_N   wall us/call   prof total   launch   load_bin   eval
       1    4096       4096        231.9        252.4     113.3      53.2     36.6
      64 1048576      16384        219.0        254.6     107.7      59.0     36.7
     256 1048576       4096        215.9        248.6     105.2      54.2     37.1
    1024 16777216     16384        252.4        286.4     135.2      59.4     37.1
    4096 16777216      4096       1084.6       1122.8     941.9      73.7     47.3

=> budget closes: launch + load_binary + eval + ~20-30 us of JitKernel.__call__
   wrapper reproduces the wall number at every point (cProfile overhead makes
   prof total slightly higher than wall; the wrapper frame itself does not
   appear because cProfile attributes its time to callees).
=> shape: flat 216-232 us from 1 to 256 blocks, then 0.04 us/block to 1024
   and 0.26 us/block from 1024 to 4096.  Not one line through the origin:
   the 4096-block point is 4.7x the 1-block point, not 4096x.
=> the slope sits inside ACL's rtKernelLaunch (launch frame absorbs 941.9 of
   the 1084.6 us at 4096 blocks); tilelang's generated launcher issues a single
   rtKernelLaunch and only calls rtMalloc/syncBlockLock when workspace_size or
   lock_num is non-zero, neither of which applies here.
=> the earlier "0.27 us/block" was a two-point fit across 1024-4096 and should
   not be extrapolated to small grids; and 939.5/1024 = 0.92, 939.5/4096 = 0.23,
   so even the launcher slope differs by segment.

